Seeded defect for tools/aot-smoke/run.sh (the BLite warning count of the Consumer publish)

Hand-made: CollectionSecondaryIndex.ConvertToIndexKey turns an int key into an IndexKey through
reflection, typeof(IndexKey).GetMethod("Create").MakeGenericMethod(value.GetType()).Invoke(...),
instead of new IndexKey(int), with #pragma warning disable IL2060, IL3050 around it so BLite.Core
builds clean. Every secondary-index write of an int property and every QueryIndexAsync bound
on one goes through it: the Consumer's idx_Count on every insert, update and query.

With it applied, run.sh fails with (osx-arm64, 2026-10-17):
    new: src/BLite.Core/Indexing/CollectionSecondaryIndex.cs(760): AOT analysis warning IL3050:
         BLite.Core.Indexing.CollectionSecondaryIndex`2.CreateThroughReflection(Object): Using member
         'System.Reflection.MethodInfo.MakeGenericMethod(Type[])' ...
    FAIL    Consumer publish: 11 BLite warnings, expected 0; 1 not registered; known: A1 x2, A3 x2, A4 x2, A5 x4
The dump stays the same: IndexKey.Create<int> is compiled into the binary anyway (the Int32
primary key uses it), so the reflection call succeeds under AOT. The warning count is what
catches the defect, as it would catch a reflection path that does fail at runtime one release
later.

Reproduce: tools/aot-smoke/run.sh --prove-seeds index-key-reflection
   or:    git apply --ignore-whitespace tools/aot-smoke/seeds/aot-smoke.index-key-reflection.patch && tools/aot-smoke/run.sh
Restore:   git checkout -- src

The source file uses CRLF line endings; apply with --ignore-whitespace if the patch was
normalised. Never commit the seeded state.

